# Your HR Team Is Buried in Spreadsheets

Onboarding, leave tracking, and payroll inputs are all manual, error-prone, and slow.

As headcount grows, spreadsheet-based HR processes stop scaling. Onboarding checklists get missed, leave balances go out of sync, and payroll inputs require manual reconciliation every cycle, all of which eats HR team time that should go toward people, not paperwork.

Symptoms:
- Onboarding steps missed because there's no single checklist system
- Leave balances that don't match between what employees and HR see
- Payroll inputs requiring manual cross-checking every cycle
- No self-service option for employees to check basic HR information

Our solution: We implement or integrate an HRMS that automates onboarding workflows, leave and attendance tracking, and payroll input handoff, with employee self-service so routine questions don't land in HR's inbox.

FAQs:

Q: Can this integrate with our existing payroll provider?
A: In most cases yes, HRMS platforms are built to hand off structured payroll inputs to external payroll processors rather than replace them.

Q: How long does implementation take?
A: It depends on process complexity and data migration scope, but a phased rollout starting with onboarding and leave tracking can go live relatively quickly.